  "worked_solution": "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
